        <p>A fire broke out in the stores of the Runcorn Old Soapery of the United Alkali Company on Tuesday evening. The stores contained many barrels of oil, and in three minutes from the alerm being raised the place was blazing wildly. The works brigade got out their hose and were soon joined by the Runcorn town brigade The flames were prevented from spreading, the stores being allowed to burn itself out. The cause of the tire is supposed to have been the dropping of a lighted lamp by a workman. The damage amounts to £3OO. The old soapery was the scene of a great tire in 1873 ; £BO,OOO damage was done in a few hours.</p>
