        <p>C 0 UN TY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON The Health Committee require the services of a LADY INSPECTOR who shall act as Health Visitor and, if required, as Inspector of Midwives. Candidates must hold certificate‘of at least three years training as Nurse in a general hospital and must also possess the certificate of the Central Midwives Board. Salary £BO per annum rising to £lOO by annual increments of £5. £5 annual allowance for uniform. Applications, to be made on forms to be obtained from this office, together with copies of not more than three testimonials, to be sent in to the undersigned not later than Wednesday January 29th 1913 and endorsed " Health Visitor." J. COOTE HIBBERT, Health Department Medical Officer of Health. - 78 Sankey-stieet, Warrington..</p>
        <p>NATIONAL HEALTH INSURANCE. MEDICAL BENEFIT. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. The INSURANCE COMMITTEE for the County Borough of Warrington hereby give NOTICE to insured persons resident within the above-named area that arrangements have been made for the administration of Medical Benefit by a panel of doctors which has been formed for the area. Insured persons resident in this area who desire to obtain medical attendance and treatment from a doctor on the panel should present their Medical Ticket to one of the doctors, a list of whom may be seen at anY Post Office in this area, or at the Town Hall. Medicine, etc.,when ordered by a doctor on the panel, can be obtained-from any of the persons or firms who have undertaken the supply of drugs and appliances, .a list of whom may also be seen at any Post Office in this area or at the Town Hall. Insured persons can if they choose apply to receive medical treatment through the approved Institution also appearing on the list above referred to. Application must be made on the form provided for the purpose. This can be obtained from the nearest Officer of Customs and Excise, whose address will be given upon enquiry at any Post Office, from the Office of the Institution or from the Town Hall. Insured persons may also make application (on a form which may be obtained at the Town Hall) to the Insurance Committee to be allowed to make their own arrangements. secretaries of Branches of approved Societies, situate in this area, are requested to make application for forms and lists above referred to at the Town Hall. Any further information can be obtained upon application to the local branch of the insured person's Approved Society, or to the nearest Officer of Customs and Excise, whose address will be given on enquiry at any Post Office, or by writing to the Clerk to the Insurance Committee at the Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— HOUSING, TOWN PLANNING, &amp;a., ACT, 1900. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that by an instru- ment (of which a copy is appended hereto), dated the .Bth day of December, 1912, tbe Local Government Board have given authority to the Corporation of Warrington to prepare a Town Planning Scheme under the provisions of part 2 of the above Act. The Instrument giving such authority may be inspected and any necessary explanation or information with regard thereto may be obtained, without payment of any fee, at my office during the hours of 10 a.m. and 5 p.m. on an, week-day (Saturday 10 a.m. to 12.30 p.m.), pending the preparation or adoption of the schemo. The Corporation now propose to prepare a scheme, and any person interested or affected desiring to be beard in reference to such proposal should give notice in writing to sue within 21 days from the date hereof. Dated this eleventh day of January. 1913. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— EDUCATION COMMITTEE. TENDERS are invited for the supply of : (a) BRUSHES (b) FIREWOOD and SAWDUST (o) PAILS, &amp;o.; (d) SOAP and (e) For the CLEANING OF SCHOOL WINDOWS. Forms of tender may be obtained, and necessary samples seen, at the Education Office, Sankey Street. All tenders are to be returned to the Education Office, by the 18th January, 1913. Education Office, J. MOORE MURRAY, M.Sc., Warrington. Secretary and Director.</p>
        <p>NATIONAL INSURANCE ACT. FREE CHOICE OF DOCTOR. -- EVERY INSURED PERSON who desires to be attended 1)5, a Doctor NOT ON THE Panel should apply to the Local Insurance Committee for permission to make his own arrrngemepts and if this is obtained he will be entitled to have repaid to him a definite sum of money. If you desire to do this send your Red Insurance Ticket to the Clerk to the Insurance Committee. Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
        <p>HOUSING, TOWN PLANNING, &amp;c., ACT, 1009. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. ViIIIEREAS the Mayor, Aldermen and Burgesses of the County Borough of Warrington, acting by the Council (hereinafter referred to as "the Corporation") asied a resolution on the fourth day of June, 1912, applying to us, the Local Government Board, to authorize the Corporation to prepare a Town Planning Scheme in respect of an area situate within the said borough and enclosed within a pink border upon a certain 'Dap marked "Map No. 2," referred to in the said resolution: AND WHEREAS the rtsolution of the Corporation, tegether with a copy of the map marked "Map No 2," referred to therein, has been transmitted to ug, and we have inquired into the application and into the circumstances connected therewith: NOW THEREFORE we eo hereby, under the pro- visions of sub-sections (2) and (3) of Section 31 of the Housing Town Planning, &amp;c., Act, 1909, authorize the Corporation to prepare a Town Planning Scheme with reference to the land (including land already built upon and land not likely to be used for building pur- poses), to which the aforesaid application relates, with the exception of so much of the land coloured pink as is included in an area bounded on the north-west by the Cheshire Lines Railway, on the north-east by Orford- road, on the south-east by Padgate-lane, and on the south-west by Gorsey-lane. AND WE do further authorize the Corporation in the preparation of the scheme as aforesaid to provide therein for the demolition or alteration of any of the buildings on the land included in the area in respect of which a scheme may be prepared as aforesaid, so far as may be necessary for carrying the scheme into effect. UIVEN under the Seal of Office of the Local Government Board this eighteenth day of December, 1912. • NOEL T, KERSHAW, Assietant Secretary.</p>
