        <p>by reductions under other heads. And it may mean all the difference between colonial independence and a really united Empire. It was only when the repeated offers of the Colonies had been refused by Mr Churchill with a rudeness which I have never been able entirely to understand or to excuse, that Sir Wilfrid Laurier began to turn his eyes in other directions. And it was only the magnificent loyalty ot our Canadian sons and daughters which prevented Canada"from becoming a mere commerbial adjunct of the United States." The golden doors of opportunity are now open once again. " The Lady of the snows ' has given us three dreadnoughts as an emergency con- tribution to the navy, and she declares her willingness to consider a more permanent and effective imperial organization both for defence and for trade. If we still decline to listen to her strong young voice ; if we still allow ourselves to be deluded by selfish appeals to our stomachs ; if we shut our eyes to the great vision which inspires our dreams, we may—like poor blind Samson, pull the pillars of the Empire we have built, about our ears, and,like him, perish in the ruins we have made. Believe me," This dear loaf cry is simply a bogey dressed up to frighten the weak-minded, and it has now become not merely a bogey, but a dishonest bogey." I, at any rate, refuse to be frightened by it, and I trust the manhood of England will assert itself and show to all the world that it can "think imperially" ; and that, if necessary, it is even pre- pared to make some sacrifice for the sake of the grandest ideal which has ever inspired an English statesman.—Believe me, faithfully yours, Market Gate Chambers, ARTHUR BENNRTT Warriugton, Sth January, 1913. LIBERAL ASSOCIATION. NATIONAL HEALTH INSURANCE ACT BENEFITS CELEBRATION. In celebration of the coming into operation of the benefits of the National Insurance Act a tea and grand concert will be held in Parr Hsll on Thursday next the 16th January at 6.45. A splendid programme has been arranged. We are desired to point out the altered condition under which the offer of a silver spoon and large photograph of the parents and child is made by Mr. A. H. Crosfield. Since the condition was decided upon, Mr. Masterman, Financial Secre- tary to the Treasury, in answer to a question put to him in the House of Commons, stated that an employed contributor was entitled to maternity benefit for any child born after twelve o'clock midnight on Sunday, January 12th, if be has been an insured person for 26 weeks, and 26</p>
